After you have finished creating your simulation model, you can start running experiments with it. A
simulation run always has to end. Many models might continue running after the processes, which interest
you, have been simulated, for example to simulate failures, etc. When you use the method stop of the
EventController in your simulation model, you have to call the method endSim of the ExperimentManager
at the appropriate place. Instead, you can also set the duration of the simulation, by either entering an End
time in the EventController or setting it with the attribute End.
